Z||000000||chris6878||11-12-1999||07:04 PM||||Hey Guys...<P>I just finished installing my newly rebuild v6 in my 85 gt. I hooked all my wiring up and when i hook the wires on the starter i get a spark or something and smells like something is burning...  when i do this the lights inside the car barely come on...  but i didnt leave it connected long...  what could the problem be??  a ground or what?  <P>Oh yeah...  what is that box above the auto tranny that has plugins on it.. and a cable that connects to the butterfly next to the gas feed and passing gear cable....       <P>thanks guys...   hopefully i will have the thing running in the morning   YAHOOOOOO||||reg||5
Z||000001||Cooter||11-12-1999||08:14 PM||||When the engine was replaced in my parts car, the guy hooked up one set of wires that were supposed to go to the starter's main battery connection to a ground instead. It looks like an easy mistake to make because the wires were pretty nasty and black so he thought they were grounds. You may have done the same thing.||||reg||1
Z||000002||chris6878||11-13-1999||01:06 AM||||Thanks Cooter...   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||12
Z||000003||Raydar||11-13-1999||11:17 AM||||Chris, sounds like the box with the cable and plug-ins is the cruise control. It will have a vacuum canister that looks like a small coffee can. ||||reg||1
Z||000004||chris6878||11-13-1999||12:18 PM||||My car isnt equipped with cruise control...  according to the vin # it is suppose to be a 85 se 4cyl..   but it has a V6 so (and it looks like an 85 Gt)..     any thing is possible... and there isnt a vacumn connected, just that cable...   and it has 3 adustment screws on it to adjust something...<P>thanks<BR>chris||||reg||5
Z||000005||chris6878||11-13-1999||08:13 PM||||Hey Guys....      yeah...  me again...<P>I messed around with the wiring on my car today.. i found what wire is grounded.. i think...     when i touch the battery cable to the terminal..  on the wires in the wiring harness was getting hot (i mean hot). So i traced this wire down...   it was one of two wires that are on a connecter that go to the starter..   (in the same spot as the main cable)     will i have to take the wiring harness back out and check it or is there a better explanation...  all of the sensor plugins are already disconnected...   <P>thanks guys...||||reg||3
